## 3. Logical Relationships (as per example)

```
G1 -> G1.1, G1.2, G1.3, G1.4, G1.5 [AND][sequential]
- Justification: All transport steps must be executed; the sequence reflects real‑world order.

G1.3 -> G1.3.1, G1.3.2 [AND][sequential]
- Justification: Drive before door opening.

G1.4 -> G1.4.1, G1.4.2 [AND][sequential]
- Justification: Decide before execution.

G1.4.2 -> G1.4.2.1, G1.4.2.2 [FALLBACK(G1.4.2.1, G1.4.2.2)]
- Justification: Attempt table delivery first; fallback to tray retrieval.

G1.5 -> G1.5.1 [AND][sequential]
- Justification: Retrieval of dishes follows door opening.

G1.5.1 -> AT8a, AT8b, AT8c [FALLBACK(FALLBACK(AT8a, AT8b), AT8c)]
- Justification: Try unassisted first; fallback to robot‑robot or robot‑human as needed.

G1.3.2 -> AT4a, AT4b [FALLBACK(AT4a, AT4b)]
- Justification: Robot attempts; if fails, human opens.

G1.4.2.2 -> AT7a, AT7b, AT7c, AT7d [AND][sequential]
- Justification: Inform, fetch, log, alert must occur in order.
```

